\section{Close the Clobber Summary over Recursive Calls}

For private direct calls, a summary can avoid evacuating a volatile
register that is never touched. Compute the closure only after the
machine register choices and link-time target sets are known. In this
simple model each function supplies a mask of all volatile units it
may write outside calls, including helper sequences and prologues.
The mask represents possible writes regardless of whether an internal
save later restores the unit; it is conservative rather than minimal.
Each call has a complete finite target set or the ordinary public ABI
mask. Use the public mask also for interposable code without a proved
private target. Call-site instructions outside the call itself are
included in the local mask.

\begin{sudocode}[Fixed point over machine-level clobbers]
\ForAll{private functions $f$}
  \State $S[f]\gets local[f]$ \Comment{Start with actual writes}
\EndFor
\Repeat
  \State $changed\gets\mathrm{false}$
  \ForAll{$f$ and call sites $c$ in $f$}
    \State $M\gets$ union of $S[t]$ over known targets of $c$
    \If{targets are not complete}
      \State $M\gets public[c]$ \Comment{Linkage limits trust}
    \EndIf
    \State grow $S[f]$ by $M$, setting $changed$ on new bits
  \EndFor
\Until{$changed$ is false}
\State \Return $S$
\end{sudocode}

On a toy ABI let the volatile units be 0, 1, and 2. Let $a$ write
unit 0 and call $b$, and $b$ write 1 and possibly recurse through
$a$. Both summaries settle at $\{0,1\}$. A caller of $a$ can leave
the value 73 in unit 2; a test should read 73 even after a terminating
recursive path. Add an unresolved call in $b$ and both masks become
$\{0,1,2\}$. Require the caller to provide another home for 73 in
that fixture, then drive the unknown target to actually write unit 2.

The invariant at convergence is containment of every direct write and
all reachable call summaries. Each successful growth adds a bit from
a finite universe, so recursion cannot prevent termination. If an
allocator changes a callee after recording the masks, rebuild or
invalidate dependent callers; closure over stale local masks is not a
preservation proof.
